From: =?UTF-8?q?Niccol=C3=B2=20Venerandi?= <niccolo@venerandi.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:34:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libtaskmanager: notify views when a new transient activates
 its parent

A window that is already active when it appears, such as the modal
dialog of an XWayland app, made its parent the active task without
emitting a change, so the task stayed unhighlighted. Emit it now.

BUG: 512159
---
 libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp b/libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp
index ed0b90cbbf..e2e860fc09 100644
--- a/libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp
+++ b/libtaskmanager/waylandtasksmodel.cpp
@@ -623,7 +623,11 @@ void WaylandTasksModel::Private::addWindow(PlasmaWindow *window)
         }

         lastActivated[effectiveActive] = QDateTime::currentDateTime();
-        activeWindow = effectiveActive;
+        PlasmaWindow *previousActive = std::exchange(activeWindow, effectiveActive);
+        if (previousActive != effectiveActive) {
+            this->dataChanged(previousActive, IsActive);
+            this->dataChanged(effectiveActive, IsActive);
+        }
     }

     QObject::connect(window, &PlasmaWindow::activeChanged, q, [window, this] {
